        </subsection>

        <!-- Part 3 -->
        <subsection xml:id="subsec-day14-verify-stage">
            <title>Part 3: Verify the Wiring, Stage the Project</title>

            <!-- DELIVERY 2: connecting prose.  OWES, by id: a paragraph on
                 the hardware-vs-software split that act-day14-stage's first
                 task establishes (if whoami_test.c still prints, Tuesday's
                 wiring survived and everything after today is software).
                 The two-main() explanation below is written now because the
                 staging slide asserts the rescue line. -->
            <p>
                A project can only have one <c>main()</c>, and after you add
                <c>accel_test.c</c> your project will contain two: the new
                test program's, and <c>whoami_test.c</c>'s.  The fix is the
                one from Day 1x: exclude the file you are done with from the
                build.  Right-click <c>whoami_test.c</c>, choose
                <em>Resource Configurations → Exclude from Build</em>,
                click <em>Select All</em> so both Debug and Release exclude
                the file, then click OK
                (<xref ref="fig-exclude-dialog"/>).  If your build fails
                with <c>multiple definition of 'main'</c>, or of
                <c>lsm303_AccelRegisterRead</c>, which both files define,
                you skipped this step.
            </p>

